fix(health booking DOB): autocomplete fecha de nacimiento from the padrón when available

Root cause: the padrón data layer carried no birth date. The `padron` table has
only cedula/nombre/papellido/sapellido, and `padron_lookup` returned only those,
so the verifier always returned dob:null — the booking then always asked DOB
manually. The route -> verifier -> booking auto-fill plumbing was already correct.

Fix (server-side only, padrón stays private — no auth gate, verification flow
untouched):
- Migration 053: add padron.fecha_nacimiento (+ staging + swap fn) and return it
  from the SECURITY DEFINER padron_lookup RPC (EXECUTE = service_role only).
- Verifier lookup now returns the DOB (normalized YYYY-MM-DD) and derives isAdult
  from it (falls back to true = electoral roll is 18+ when no DOB).

Behavior: when the padrón has a birth date for the cédula, health bookings
autocomplete the DOB (self field locks; beneficiary field prefills) for both
self and third-party. When the cédula isn't in the padrón, or the loaded roll
has no DOB, the field is asked manually (unchanged fallback).

NOTE: the bare TSE electoral roll has no birth date — DOB autocompletes only once
a DOB-bearing dataset is loaded into padron.fecha_nacimiento.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
